❮ ArrayList Methods

TheensureCapacity()method increases the capacity of a list to a specified amount, if necessary.

This method does not have a visible effect but it can make code more efficient.

When methods such asadd()andaddAll()are called, if the capacity of a list is not large enough then some extra work is done to add enough space for the new items. It takes a bit of time to do this, so having this happen with everyadd()call is not ideal.

If you know approximately how many items you are going to add, theensureCapacity()method allows you to increase the capacity of the list just once for multipleadd()calls.

